  "duration": 17,
  "audio": {
    "silent": true,
    "_why": "a demo of one optical effect. The film's only claim is what the glass does to the frame behind it, and a bed track would ask the viewer to read the cut instead of the refraction."
  },
  "_brief": {
    "SUBJECT": "3D glass shapes, the After Effects way, done in this engine",
    "PAYOFF": "the glass is not a frosted panel: it bends and splits the real frame behind it",
    "SPECTACLE": "beat 3, the ring: the same band of type refracted twice, once on each wall of the tube, with the dispersion fringes wide open",
    "NOT": "no gradient hero, no floating cards, no purple, no stock 3D render. Every pixel inside a shape is the scene's own backdrop, displaced."
  },
